+- **Overrides in a staging or production release:** both `ApiClient` and
+  the realtime handshake open direct TLS hops through
+  `SslPinning.secureConnect` to refuse redirects that leave TLS. Those hops
+  use the default context when pinning is off, or the fresh pinned context
+  when pinning is on; they do not consult a context or
+  `badCertificateCallback` installed through `HttpOverrides`. An override
+  that works in debug or profile therefore does not configure release TLS.
+  With pinning off, load a private CA with
+  `SecurityContext.defaultContext.setTrustedCertificatesBytes(...)`, and
+  load your client chain and key into that same default context before
+  making requests. With pinning on, customize the contexts in `SslPinning`
+  instead. Do not rely on an override to bypass the release certificate
+  policy.
 
